FSL's standard images and topup's settings in larmorx-nc
========================================================

This directory holds three files of FSL's standard-space data, copied byte for byte from FSL
6.0.7.23's data package fsl-data_standard 2208.0 (FSL's conda channel,
https://fsl.fmrib.ox.ac.uk/fsldownloads/fslconda/public/noarch/fsl-data_standard-2208.0-0.tar.bz2,
SHA-256 2faefb4d366b6427cbf4e5c3e54c63c040ec9bcfe11b1f10848f89a1571b828a), where they are
${FSLDIR}/data/standard/<file>. They are the images FSL's bet script (its options -S, -B, -A,
-A2) and standard_space_roi read, and larmorx-nc's replicas of those scripts read them from here
when no FSL installation is given.

It also holds six files of FSL's topup settings (etc/flirtsch/b02b0.cnf, b02b0_1.cnf,
b02b0_2.cnf, b02b0_4.cnf, b02b0_7T.cnf, test_acqp.cnf), copied byte for byte from FSL 6.0.7.23's
package fsl-topup 2203.5 (FSL's conda channel,
https://fsl.fmrib.ox.ac.uk/fsldownloads/fslconda/public/linux-64/fsl-topup-2203.5-ha905fa9_6.conda,
SHA-256 24381a8ab0d7410bc86c440a57666a9c166aef3a48fcf0fb1080a81a60d8909f), where they are
${FSLDIR}/etc/flirtsch/<file>: the settings topup --config=<name> reads, which larmorx-nc's topup
replica and larmorx's port of sdcflows read from here when no FSL installation is given.
MANIFEST.tsv lists each file, its size and its SHA-256.

